dwm - dynamic window manager
============================
dwm is an extremely fast, small, and dynamic window manager for X.

This is a personal build of dwm with a set of patches applied on top
of the upstream source (see "Patches" below).


Requirements
------------
In order to build dwm you need the Xlib header files.

Optional, depending on the features you use:

- a compositor such as picom or xcompmgr, for the focus-based window opacity
- dwmblocks-async (a build that supports statuscmd), for the clickable status bar
- clipmenu, for the clipboard history binding
- slock, for the lock screen binding
- the helper scripts used by the media keys (sb-volume, sb-mic,
  sb-brightness) found in my dots repo and the screenshot binding (screenshot script in the dots repo too)


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dwm is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dwm (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install

Note: config.h is tracked directly in this repository (not
config.def.h), and `make clean` also removes leftover patch artifacts
(.orig and .rej files).


Running dwm
-----------
Add the following line to your .xinitrc to start dwm using startx:

    exec dwm

In order to connect dwm to a specific display, make sure that
the DISPLAY environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec dwm

(This will start dwm on display :1 of the host foo.bar.)

In order to display status info in the bar, you can do something
like this in your .xinitrc:

    while xsetroot -name "`date` `uptime | sed 's/.*,//'`"
    do
    	sleep 1
    done &
    exec dwm


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of dwm is done by editing config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.


Patches
-------
The following patches from https://dwm.suckless.org/patches/ are
applied, roughly in the order they were added:

- statuscmd
- vanitygaps
- colorbar
- restartsig
- hide_vacant_tags
- actualfullscreen
- alwayscenter
- preventfocusshift
- attachaside


Keybindings
-----------
The full list lives in config.h. The main ones:

    Mod + Space			dmenu launcher
    Mod + q			terminal
    Mod + w			close window
    Mod + f			toggle fullscreen
    Mod + b			toggle bar
    Mod + c			clipboard history (clipmenu)
    Mod + x			lock screen
    Mod + = / -			increase / decrease gaps
    Mod + g			toggle gaps
    Mod + Shift + g		reset gaps to default
    Mod + Shift + q		restart dwm
    Mod + Shift + backspace	quit dwm
    Print			screenshot (monitor)
    Shift + Print		screenshot (region)
    Mod + Print			screenshot (window)
    Volume/brightness		XF86 media keys, via the sb-* scripts
